# Tips are the prompt — never bypass the tip loader

System prompts for anything that GENERATES with Gemma are assembled at run time
from NAMS core-tip Preference rows. Code is the seed, NAMS is the source at
run time. This is a design decision (2026-08-19, commit 88171ec; restored for
S2 on 2026-11-18 after the S1/S2 rewrite dropped it), not an implementation
detail to clean up.

- `CORE_S2_TIPS`, `CORE_PLAYER_TIPS`, `CORE_ANALYST_TIPS`,
  `CORE_FAILURE_ANALYST_TIPS` in `agent/modes.py` are the seed tables.
  `ensure_core_tips` heals NAMS to them. Seed numbers stay below 500;
  500+ is the agent's. `get_core_tips` fails on any other category.
  Keep all of that. The failure-analyst prefix is `core_fa_`.
- Every harness or notebook that generates (play, testing_s2,
  testing_learn_to_look, the failure analyst) loads its system prompt
  with `load_s2_prompt(client)` / `load_scene_prompts(client)` /
  `load_failure_analyst_prompt(client)`. Importing `SYSTEM_PROMPT_S2`
  to generate at run time is a bug. t1 greps for it.
- No fallback to the constant when NAMS is down. Fail (no-fuzzy-fallbacks).
- Tip writing stays: the `[TIP: ...]` line, `parse_tip_lines`, `add_s2_tip`,
  `replace_core_tip`, `delete_core_tip`, the play.ipynb Tips panel, and the
  debrief's `[WRITE_TIP]`. The tool assigns the category, never the agent.
- Training and eval build prompts with the same `assemble_s2_prompt`, so a
  training prompt is indistinguishable from a loaded one. Fabricated saved
  tips are part of the fake-NAMS context, drawn once per batch.
- `s1_s2_design_notes/cursor-recommendations.md` section 6 is superseded on
  this point: OBS: and the analyst round stay out of the S2 loop; NAMS tips
  stay in.
